---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Website Build Brief
description: The intake for a 406 Front Desk website build. Eight short steps, saved as you go, so we can build something close on the first draft instead of guessing.
pageCss: build-brief
permalink: /build-brief/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
noindex: true   # client-only link, sent after the yes -- not a marketing page
---
{#
  Website Build Brief — the custom-HTML replacement for GHL form XxclnFTTfAcAmdLNPC1I.

  WHY THIS EXISTS AS CUSTOM HTML:
  The spec's headline requirement is 8 steps. A GHL Form is single-page — multi-step is
  a Survey feature — and the Survey rebuild was blocked behind two unknowns (file
  upload support, and whether the 55 custom fields could be reused). Custom HTML gets
  the 8 steps, the file upload, save-and-resume on a 56-field form, and the design
  picker as a step, with no Survey rebuild and neither unknown.
  See wiki/synthesis/Website Build Brief — Form vs Survey Decision.

  FIELDS ARE GENERATED, NOT TYPED. src/_data/buildBrief.json comes from the live GHL
  API via scripts/sync-build-brief.mjs. A wrong fieldKey is accepted silently by GHL
  and the answer is dropped, so the keys must never be hand-written.

  NO A2P CONSENT BLOCK. This is a client form, not lead capture — the phone is a
  contact field only, and the opt-in lives on the public opt-in page. Both default GHL
  consent checkboxes were deliberately deleted when the original was built.
#}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/directions-fonts.css?v={{ buildStamp }}" />

<div class="header-band">
  <span class="header-eyebrow">Website build</span>
  <h1>Your build brief</h1>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="bb-intro">
    <p>
      This is everything I need to build you something that is close on the first draft instead of a
      guess. Eight short steps, about ten to fifteen minutes.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>It saves as you go</strong> — on this device, in this browser. Close the tab and come back
      to the same link and you will pick up where you left off. Nothing is sent until you hit submit on
      the last step.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="bb-rail" id="bbRail" aria-label="Progress">
    {% for s in buildBrief.sections %}
    <li class="bb-rail__step" data-step="{{ s.n }}"><span class="bb-rail__n">{{ s.n }}</span><span class="bb-rail__t">{{ s.title }}</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  <form id="bbForm" class="bb-form" novalidate autocomplete="on">
    {# Honeypot. A real person never fills this; bots fill everything. #}
    <div class="bb-hp" aria-hidden="true">
      <label>Company website<input type="text" name="website_hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
    </div>

    {% for s in buildBrief.sections %}
    <fieldset class="bb-step" data-step="{{ s.n }}" {% if s.n != 1 %}hidden{% endif %}>
      <legend class="bb-step__legend">
        <span class="bb-step__count">Step {{ s.n }} of {{ buildBrief.sections | length }}</span>
        <span class="bb-step__title">{{ s.title }}</span>
      </legend>
      <p class="bb-step__blurb">{{ s.blurb }}</p>

      {% if s.n == 1 %}
      {# Standard contact fields — these are the contact record itself, not custom fields. #}
      <div class="bb-field">
        <label class="bb-label" for="full_name">Your name <span class="bb-req">required</span></label>
        <input class="bb-input" type="text" id="full_name" name="full_name" required autocomplete="name" />
      </div>
      <div class="bb-field">
        <label class="bb-label" for="email">Best email <span class="bb-req">required</span></label>
        <p class="bb-help">Where drafts and links get sent.</p>
        <input class="bb-input" type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>
      <div class="bb-field">
        <label class="bb-label" for="phone">Best cell <span class="bb-req">required</span></label>
        <p class="bb-help">Where I'll text you during the build. No marketing, ever.</p>
        <input class="bb-input" type="tel" id="phone" name="phone" required autocomplete="tel" />
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% for f in buildBrief.fields %}{% if f.section == s.n %}
      <div class="bb-field" data-key="{{ f.key }}">
        {% if f.key == "design_directions_picked" %}
          {# The picker, inline. This is the whole reason the form moved off GHL: a client
             points at a look instead of being told to go find three websites they like. #}
          <span class="bb-label">{{ f.label }}</span>
          <p class="bb-help">
            Pick one or two that feel right. Not a commitment — it tells me which direction to run at.
            <a href="/design-directions/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See them full size</a>.
          </p>
          <input type="hidden" name="{{ f.key }}" id="ddPicked" />
          <div class="bb-picker">
            {% for d in directions.items %}
            <button type="button" class="bb-swatch" data-code="{{ d.code }}" data-name="{{ d.name }}"
              aria-pressed="false"
              style="--d-page:{{ d.palette.page }};--d-surface:{{ d.palette.surface }};--d-ink:{{ d.palette.ink }};--d-muted:{{ d.palette.muted }};--d-accent:{{ d.palette.accent }};--d-accent-ink:{{ d.palette.accentInk }};--d-hair:{{ d.palette.hair }};--d-btn:{{ d.palette.btnLabel }};--d-fh:{{ d.type.heading.stack | safe }};--d-fb:{{ d.type.body.stack | safe }};--d-fwh:{{ d.type.heading.weight }}">
              <span class="bb-swatch__prev">
                <span class="bb-swatch__h">{{ directions.sample.headline }}</span>
                <span class="bb-swatch__p">{{ directions.sample.ctaSecondary }}</span>
                <span class="bb-swatch__btn">{{ directions.sample.ctaPrimary }}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="bb-swatch__meta"><b>{{ d.code }}</b> {{ d.name }}</span>
            </button>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        {% else %}
          <label class="bb-label" for="f_{{ f.key }}">
            {{ f.label }}{% if f.required %} <span class="bb-req">required</span>{% endif %}
          </label>
          {% if f.help %}<p class="bb-help">{{ f.help }}</p>{% endif %}

          {% if f.type == "LARGE_TEXT" %}
            <textarea class="bb-input bb-textarea" id="f_{{ f.key }}" name="{{ f.key }}" rows="4" {% if f.required %}required{% endif %}></textarea>
          {% elif f.type == "RADIO" or f.type == "SINGLE_OPTIONS" %}
            <div class="bb-options" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="f_{{ f.key }}">
              {% for o in f.options %}
              <label class="bb-option"><input type="radio" name="{{ f.key }}" value="{{ o }}" {% if f.required %}required{% endif %} /><span>{{ o }}</span></label>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% elif f.type == "CHECKBOX" or f.type == "MULTIPLE_OPTIONS" %}
            <div class="bb-options bb-options--multi" data-multi="1">
              {% for o in f.options %}
              <label class="bb-option"><input type="checkbox" name="{{ f.key }}" value="{{ o }}" /><span>{{ o }}</span></label>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% elif f.type == "FILE_UPLOAD" %}
            <input class="bb-input bb-file" type="file" id="f_{{ f.key }}" name="{{ f.key }}"
                   accept=".png,.jpg,.jpeg,.svg,.pdf,.ai,.eps,.webp" />
            <p class="bb-help bb-help--sub">Up to 4 MB. If your logo is bigger, or you have a folder of them, just email it over instead.</p>
          {% elif f.type == "DATE" %}
            <input class="bb-input" type="date" id="f_{{ f.key }}" name="{{ f.key }}" />
          {% else %}
            <input class="bb-input" type="text" id="f_{{ f.key }}" name="{{ f.key }}" {% if f.required %}required{% endif %} />
          {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        <p class="bb-error" hidden>This one's needed before the next step.</p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}

      <div class="bb-nav">
        <button type="button" class="bb-btn bb-btn--ghost" data-back {% if s.n == 1 %}hidden{% endif %}>Back</button>
        {% if s.n < 8 %}
        <button type="button" class="bb-btn" data-next>Next step</button>
        {% else %}
        <button type="submit" class="bb-btn bb-btn--go">Send my brief</button>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </fieldset>
    {% endfor %}

    <div class="bb-saved" id="bbSaved" hidden>Saved on this device</div>
  </form>

  <div class="bb-done" id="bbDone" hidden>
    <h2>That's it — thank you.</h2>
    <p id="bbDoneMsg">Your brief is in. I'll read it properly and come back to you with anything that needs a conversation before I start building.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="/js/build-brief.js?v={{ buildStamp }}" defer></script>
